.TH MKDIR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
mkdir \- create a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.BI "int mkdir(const char* " path ", mode_t " mode ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR mkdir ()
creates the directory named by
.IR path .
.I mode
specifies Linux creation permission bits, modified by the process umask
and possibly the parent directory's default ACL.
For example, 493 is the decimal value of Unix permissions 0755.
Parent directories must already exist.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged; \-1 on failure with
.B errno
set to the positive Linux error number.
.SH ERRORS
Possible errors include
.BR EEXIST ,
.BR ENOENT ,
.BR EACCES ,
and
.BR ENOSPC .
Other Linux
.BR mkdir (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Crunch
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rmdir (3crunch),
.BR mkdir (2)
